@copilot Add an explanatory code comment in this existing PR #20792 directly, with no behavior changes.

In all three JedisServerError.errorType implementations under instrumentation/jedis/jedis-2.0/javaagent, jedis-3.0/javaagent and jedis-4.0/javaagent, place these exact two lines immediately above the if (error == null || error.getClass() != JedisDataException.class) guard:

```java
// Preserve exception-class classification for dedicated Jedis exceptions.
// Only generic JedisDataException messages are parsed for Redis error prefixes.
```

This documents the deliberate classification policy: dedicated exception subclasses retain their exception class as error.type. Do not replace the exact-class check with instanceof, claim that subclasses always alter their messages, change classification or extraction logic, or modify the existing separate ASCII-decoding comments.

Keep the update limited to these three comment additions and any directly required formatting. Preserve the PR's live base, draft state and all existing code/tests. Do not create another PR, merge/rebase, change PR metadata, post replies/comments/reviews, resolve threads or request a review; the coordinator handles the completion loop. Run only the narrow relevant formatting if needed and verify that the final diff is comment-only. No new tests or behavior changes are needed for this documentation-only update. Do not wait for CI.

