@copilot Update this PR directly to simplify waiting for setup telemetry. The previous request over-specified "await and assert"; the user's settled requirement is to drain and discard setup traces, not assert their contents. Follow .github/agents/knowledge/testing-general-patterns.md and .github/instructions/java-tests.instructions.md on trace clearing.

In the Jedis 2, 3, and 4 integration tests changed by commit bcee81d99327b88dafde229cd7ce09df92788c17, replace each assertLpushTrace() call with testing.waitForTraces(1), then remove the unused assertLpushTrace() helpers. These files are instrumentation/jedis/jedis-2.0/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/jedis/v2_0/JedisClientTest.java, instrumentation/jedis/jedis-3.0/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/jedis/v3_0/Jedis30ClientTest.java, and instrumentation/jedis/jedis-4.0/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/jedis/v4_0/Jedis40ClientTest.java. Replace the setup LPUSH/SET waitAndAssertTraces blocks added in pipelineAndTransactionErrorsCompleteBatchSpans() with testing.waitForTraces(2). Retain the waits before clearing captured data, including the mid-test reset in caughtDirectConnectionServerErrorDoesNotFailSuccessfulOuterPipeline(), and use the total deterministic trace count at each point. Do not wait on batch spans that remain open until the operation under test completes.

Preserve every assertion of the actual behavior under test, including error.type, batch traces, and metrics. Keep the new ServerSocket(0) change and preserve the PR's ready-for-review state. Do not change production code, update knowledge articles or instructions, or reply to or resolve human threads. Run the narrowest applicable formatter and relevant changed tests with supported dependency variants, and report any execution limitations accurately.

